          "quote": "Let $K_0,K_1$ be smooth oriented knots in the standard oriented three-sphere $S^3$, and let $I=[0,1]$. A smooth concordance from $K_0$ to $K_1$ is the image of a smooth proper embedding $f:S^1\\times I\\to S^3\\times I$ whose lower and upper boundary circles are $K_0\\times\\{0\\}$ and $K_1\\times\\{1\\}$. The embedding has product collars at both ends: in a neighborhood of each boundary circle it is the corresponding knot embedding crossed with the interval coordinate. Orient the annulus so that its boundary, with the boundary-orientation convention, is $-K_0\\times\\{0\\}\\sqcup K_1\\times\\{1\\}$. The knots are smoothly concordant when such an annulus exists.",
